Discussion:
The 5 remaining categories carry 50 atomic fields total. The
routing decisions land them on 4 destinations:

* media (11) -> media_snapshot. Every Media* atomic has a hot
  column on media_snapshots from migrations/000170_snapshots_si.up.sql
  lines 268-302. MediaAudioVolume{,Increment,Max} -> volume_pct /
  volume_increment / volume_max. MediaNowPlaying{Album,Artist,
  Duration,Elapsed,Station,Title} -> album / artist / duration_s /
  elapsed_s / station / track_name. MediaPlayback{Source,Status}
  -> source / play_status. Durations and elapsed positions are
  seconds (SI); volumes are integer percent (the head unit reports
  the fraction-of-max already pre-scaled). UnitKind is None for
  every Media* field, so normalize.toSI is a pass-through.

* config (13) -> signal_log. CarType, EfficiencyPackage,
  EuropeVehicle, ExteriorColor, OffroadLightbarPresent,
  RemoteStartEnabled, RightHandDrive, RoofColor, SunroofInstalled,
  Trim, VehicleName, Version, WheelType. Every config field is
  identity-shaped per-VIN configuration that rarely transitions in
  the lifetime of a vehicle. signal_log is the change feed and the
  dashboard / fleet-stats consumers read the most recent value
  back from there. No hot column exists for any of them.

* prefs (1) -> signal_log. Setting24HourTime is the user dashboard
  preference for 24h vs 12h clock display. UI-shaped preference
  with no hot column; signal_log carries the change feed.

* setting_unit (4) -> unit_history. SettingChargeUnit,
  SettingDistanceUnit, SettingTemperatureUnit,
  SettingTirePressureUnit (all IsSettingUnit=true). Per ADR-004 #8,
  normalize.observeSettingUnit short-circuits the toSI + router.Route
  path for these atomics: pipeline.processOne checks meta.IsSettingUnit
  first and writes to vehicle_unit_history via unithistory.Repo.Record
  before it would otherwise dispatch. The router is NOT consulted
  for these fields at runtime.

  The YAML entry exists for accounting + discoverability: it keeps
  the 0048 reflective coverage test green (every protomodel.Signals
  atomic must have exactly one routing entry) and documents the
  observer write-path explicitly to readers. The dest is
  unit_history (not signal_log or drop) so the YAML does not lie
  about where the values land.

* metadata (21) -> drop. Deprecated_{1..3}, Experimental_{1..15},
  RearDefrostEnabled, RearDisplayHvacEnabled, Unknown. The codegen
  classifies these as metadata because they are sentinel slots in
  the upstream Tesla proto: Deprecated_* are reserved retired-field
  placeholders, Experimental_* are upstream-development reserved
  slots whose schema is not yet stable, RearDefrostEnabled and
  RearDisplayHvacEnabled are placeholder/legacy fields the protomodel
  flags as metadata (not climate) and which have no downstream
  consumer, and Unknown is the zero-value sentinel emitted when the
  codec sees a wire value the current generated proto cannot name.
  DestDrop is the declarative discard decision and ensures these
  do not pollute signal_log.

Notes on the prompt's example list:
  * "Vin" is NOT a member of pm.Signals at this proto vintage.
    The codegen does not emit a Vin SignalMeta; the VIN flows on
    the Payload header (codec.Payload.Vin), not as a wire Field.
  * "EmittedAt-like fields, payload-level frame markers" are
    likewise consumed by the codec / pipeline header (Payload.CreatedAt,
    Payload.Vin) and never reach the router as atomics. The metadata
    category in pm.Signals is the Deprecated_* / Experimental_* /
    Unknown sentinel set described above.
  * MediaTrack* / MediaSource / MediaArtist / MediaAlbumName /
    MediaPlayStatus / MediaVolume in the prompt are aspirational
    naming; the actual pm.Signals Media* fields use the
    MediaAudioVolume{,Max,Increment} / MediaNowPlaying{Title,
    Artist,Album,Station,Duration,Elapsed} / MediaPlayback{Source,
    Status} naming. The routing entries below use the actual names.
  * GuiCharge* prefs do not exist in pm.Signals at this proto
    vintage. The single member of the prefs category is
    Setting24HourTime.

No classifier ambiguity:
  * pm.Signals shows ZERO media / config / prefs / setting_unit /
    metadata fields that overlap any prior routed category. The
    routing.yaml loader's duplicate-field validator
    (TestLoaderRejectsDuplicateField) provides structural
    enforcement; no duplicates were introduced by this prompt.

